# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Simulate the $4 \\times 4$ lattice {#simulate-the-4-times-4-lattice}"
msgstr "Simuler le réseau $4 \\times 4$ {#simulate-the-4-times-4-lattice}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For the $4 \\times 4$ lattice, you can do both: compute the exact state at every coupling, and sample every circuit with 10,000 shots, as an experiment would. The shots are stored with shape (batches, shots, qubits), the same layout as the randomizations in the hardware data. Here all 10,000 shots form a single batch, so the bootstrap over batches adds no shot noise, and the error bars in the next plot show only the spread between marginal positions.\n"
msgstr "Pour le réseau $4 \\times 4$, tu peux faire les deux : calculer l'état exact à chaque couplage, et échantillonner chaque circuit avec 10 000 shots, comme le ferait une expérience. Les shots sont stockés avec la forme (lots, shots, qubits), la même disposition que les randomisations dans les données matérielles. Ici, les 10 000 shots forment un seul lot, donc le bootstrap sur les lots n'ajoute aucun bruit de shots, et les barres d'erreur du graphique suivant ne montrent que la dispersion entre les positions marginales.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "2. What to measure and how to estimate it {#2-what-to-measure-and-how-to-estimate-it}"
msgstr "2. Que mesurer et comment l'estimer {#2-what-to-measure-and-how-to-estimate-it}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "The IPR and the collision entropy {#the-ipr-and-the-collision-entropy}"
msgstr "L'IPR et l'entropie de collision {#the-ipr-and-the-collision-entropy}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For a marginal $A$ of $n_A$ qubits with bitstring distribution $p_A(a)$, the quantity to estimate is the inverse participation ratio (IPR) of the marginal distribution, and from it the collision entropy:\n"
msgstr "Pour une marginale $A$ de $n_A$ qubits avec une distribution de chaînes de bits $p_A(a)$, la quantité à estimer est le taux de participation inverse (IPR) de la distribution marginale, et à partir de lui l'entropie de collision :\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\mathrm{IPR}_A = \\sum_a p_A(a)^2, \\qquad S_2[A] = -\\log_2 \\mathrm{IPR}_A\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\mathrm{IPR}_A = \\sum_a p_A(a)^2, \\qquad S_2[A] = -\\log_2 \\mathrm{IPR}_A\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "$\\mathrm{IPR}_A$ is also the probability that two shots agree on the marginal. A product state has $\\mathrm{IPR}_A = 1$, and a random state has $\\mathrm{IPR}_A \\approx 2^{-n_A}$, so $S_2$ climbs from 0 to about $n_A$ bits as the marginal becomes random.\n"
msgstr "$\\mathrm{IPR}_A$ est aussi la probabilité que deux shots coïncident sur la marginale. Un état produit a $\\mathrm{IPR}_A = 1$, et un état aléatoire a $\\mathrm{IPR}_A \\approx 2^{-n_A}$, donc $S_2$ passe de 0 à environ $n_A$ bits à mesure que la marginale devient aléatoire.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Estimator 1: count pairs of shots {#estimator-1-count-pairs-of-shots}"
msgstr "Estimateur 1 : compter les paires de shots {#estimator-1-count-pairs-of-shots}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "> **Question.** How do you estimate this quantity from your shots?\n"
msgstr "> **Question.** Comment estimes-tu cette quantité à partir de tes shots ?\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The naive estimator computes each $p(a)$ from the shots as $\\hat p(a) = n_a / N$, then sums $\\sum_a \\hat p(a)^2$.\n"
"This estimator is biased.\n"
msgstr ""
"L'estimateur naïf calcule chaque $p(a)$ à partir des shots comme $\\hat p(a) = n_a / N$, puis somme $\\sum_a \\hat p(a)^2$.\n"
"Cet estimateur est biaisé.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "$\\sum_a n_a^2 / N^2$ counts every shot as agreeing with itself, which pushes the estimate up: on average it gives $\\mathrm{IPR}_A + (1 - \\mathrm{IPR}_A)/N$ instead of $\\mathrm{IPR}_A$. Since $\\mathrm{IPR}_A$ is the probability that two shots agree, count only pairs of *different* shots:\n"
msgstr "$\\sum_a n_a^2 / N^2$ compte chaque shot comme coïncidant avec lui-même, ce qui tire l'estimation vers le haut : en moyenne il donne $\\mathrm{IPR}_A + (1 - \\mathrm{IPR}_A)/N$ au lieu de $\\mathrm{IPR}_A$. Comme $\\mathrm{IPR}_A$ est la probabilité que deux shots coïncident, compte seulement les paires de shots *différents* :\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\widehat{\\mathrm{IPR}}_A = \\frac{\\sum_a n_a (n_a - 1)}{N (N - 1)}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\widehat{\\mathrm{IPR}}_A = \\frac{\\sum_a n_a (n_a - 1)}{N (N - 1)}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This is unbiased, and it is what `ipr_from_shots` below computes.\n"
msgstr "Il est sans biais, et c'est ce que calcule `ipr_from_shots` ci-dessous.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Estimator 2: Parseval expansion {#estimator-2-parseval-expansion}"
msgstr "Estimateur 2 : développement de Parseval {#estimator-2-parseval-expansion}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The IPR can also be written through the parities $\\langle Z_S \\rangle$ of all nonempty subsets $S$ of the marginal:\n"
msgstr "L'IPR peut aussi s'écrire à l'aide des parités $\\langle Z_S \\rangle$ de tous les sous-ensembles non vides $S$ de la marginale :\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\Large\n"
"\\mathrm{IPR}_A = 2^{-n_A}\\Bigl(1 + \\sum_{\\emptyset \\neq S \\subseteq A} \\langle Z_S \\rangle^2\\Bigr)\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\Large\n"
"\\mathrm{IPR}_A = 2^{-n_A}\\Bigl(1 + \\sum_{\\emptyset \\neq S \\subseteq A} \\langle Z_S \\rangle^2\\Bigr)\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This form matters because error mitigation methods such as PEA work on expectation values, not on probabilities.\n"
"**One qubit:** The outcome probabilities are $p(0) = (1 + \\langle Z \\rangle)/2$ and $p(1) = (1 - \\langle Z \\rangle)/2$, so\n"
msgstr ""
"Cette forme est importante, car les méthodes de mitigation d'erreurs comme PEA travaillent sur des valeurs moyennes, pas sur des probabilités.\n"
"**Un qubit :** Les probabilités des résultats sont $p(0) = (1 + \\langle Z \\rangle)/2$ et $p(1) = (1 - \\langle Z \\rangle)/2$, donc\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\Large\n"
"\\mathrm{IPR} = p(0)^2 + p(1)^2 = \\frac{1 + \\langle Z \\rangle^2}{2}\n"
"$$\n"
"**A $2 \\times 2$ marginal:** With its qubits labeled $a, b, c, d$, the marginal has $2^4 - 1 = 15$ parities: 4 single qubits, 6 pairs, 4 triples, and the whole marginal, so\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\Large\n"
"\\mathrm{IPR} = p(0)^2 + p(1)^2 = \\frac{1 + \\langle Z \\rangle^2}{2}\n"
"$$\n"
"**Une marginale $2 \\times 2$ :** Avec ses qubits étiquetés $a, b, c, d$, la marginale a $2^4 - 1 = 15$ parités : 4 qubits individuels, 6 paires, 4 triplets et la marginale entière, donc\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\Large\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\mathrm{IPR} = \\frac{1}{16} \\Bigl(1\n"
"&+ \\langle Z_a \\rangle^2 + \\langle Z_b \\rangle^2 + \\langle Z_c \\rangle^2 + \\langle Z_d \\rangle^2 \\\\\n"
"&+ \\langle Z_a Z_b \\rangle^2 + \\langle Z_a Z_c \\rangle^2 + \\langle Z_a Z_d \\rangle^2 + \\langle Z_b Z_c \\rangle^2 + \\langle Z_b Z_d \\rangle^2 + \\langle Z_c Z_d \\rangle^2 \\\\\n"
"&+ \\langle Z_a Z_b Z_c \\rangle^2 + \\langle Z_a Z_b Z_d \\rangle^2 + \\langle Z_a Z_c Z_d \\rangle^2 + \\langle Z_b Z_c Z_d \\rangle^2 \\\\\n"
"&+ \\langle Z_a Z_b Z_c Z_d \\rangle^2 \\Bigr)\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\Large\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\mathrm{IPR} = \\frac{1}{16} \\Bigl(1\n"
"&+ \\langle Z_a \\rangle^2 + \\langle Z_b \\rangle^2 + \\langle Z_c \\rangle^2 + \\langle Z_d \\rangle^2 \\\\\n"
"&+ \\langle Z_a Z_b \\rangle^2 + \\langle Z_a Z_c \\rangle^2 + \\langle Z_a Z_d \\rangle^2 + \\langle Z_b Z_c \\rangle^2 + \\langle Z_b Z_d \\rangle^2 + \\langle Z_c Z_d \\rangle^2 \\\\\n"
"&+ \\langle Z_a Z_b Z_c \\rangle^2 + \\langle Z_a Z_b Z_d \\rangle^2 + \\langle Z_a Z_c Z_d \\rangle^2 + \\langle Z_b Z_c Z_d \\rangle^2 \\\\\n"
"&+ \\langle Z_a Z_b Z_c Z_d \\rangle^2 \\Bigr)\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

